WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.040
You have something
to give back.

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:07.580
All lives have equal value, but
we don't treat them that way.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:11.000
Just because of where
you're born in the world

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.920
has a determining
effect of whether you're

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.410
going to survive to
your fifth birthday.

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:17.330
That is not equal opportunity.

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:19.615
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.120
Over 20 years, I've
learned in philanthropy

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.420
there are so many different
ways to give: time, money,

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.640
expertise, your voice.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:32.159
I'm not going to teach
you which organizations

00:00:32.159 --> 00:00:35.430
to focus on-- that's very
personal, and that's up to you.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:38.250
But I will be offering
you a framework and a way

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.840
to think about giving.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.453
Go to where your passion is.

00:00:41.453 --> 00:00:42.870
What is the thing
that you wake up

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:44.120
thinking about in the morning?

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:45.300
You say, "Ah!

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.030
Why is this happening
in my community?

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.380
I don't believe in this!"

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:52.440
You do philanthropy
because you believe deeply

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.630
that you want to leave
the world a better place.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:57.380
[MUSIC PLAYING]

